= Robustness — Technical =

== Perturbation formulation ==
Let system performance be J(s) and perturbation δ lie in admissible set Δ.

A robustness property can be expressed generically as:

<pre>
J(s, δ) remains within acceptable set A
for all / most δ ∈ Δ
</pre>

The meaning depends on Δ, A, probability model, and dynamics.

== Network robustness ==
Network robustness measures can track:

* giant-component persistence;
* connectivity;
* flow capacity;
* dynamical function;
* cascading-failure tolerance;
* recovery trajectories.

Different measures can rank the same network differently.

== Tradeoffs ==
Robustness can trade off with efficiency, cost, flexibility, or robustness to other perturbation classes.

